正如你刚才所说，关于职业生涯有很多好东西。

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:49.259
There's a lot, it's this romantic comedy, that's the category it was put in, that's the shelf it would be on in the bookstore.
有很多，这是一部浪漫喜剧，这就是它被放入的类别，这就是它在书店的书架上。

00:08:49.259 --> 00:08:55.460
But like, we do a lot about finding yourself in other ways in your late 20s, early 30s.
但是，就像我们在 20 岁末、30 岁出头时做了很多事情，以其他方式寻找自己。

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:59.899
And I'd forgotten how many of those are good, how many episodes of that or hold their weight?
我忘记了其中有多少是好的，有多少集是有分量的？

00:08:59.899 --> 00:09:14.019
This might be waiting into kind of territory that we would dance around delicately, but I think part of wanting a good career is you want to be attractive to a mate.
这可能正在等待我们微妙地跳舞的领域，但我认为想要一份好的职业的一部分是你想要对伴侣有吸引力。

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:14.860
Yeah.
是的。

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:26.620
And you want to be able to provide for your wife and your future, your imaginary wife and your imaginary children, yeah, there's a lot that goes and they're not, what I'm saying is they're inextricably linked.
你希望能够养活你的妻子和你的未来，你想象中的妻子和你想象中的孩子，是的，有很多事情发生，但他们没有，我的意思是他们是密不可分的。

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.460
Yeah.
是的。

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:38.957
search for romance, the search for love and connection and partnership in your 20s and 30s, and your ambition and your wanting to make a name for yourself and achieve in the industry you've chosen.
寻找浪漫，寻找20多岁和30多岁的爱情、联系和伙伴关系，以及你的野心和想要在你选择的行业中成名并取得成就的愿望。

00:09:38.957 --> 00:09:43.860
Those are really woven together in ways that I don't think people talk about enough.
这些确实以我认为人们谈论得不够多的方式交织在一起。

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.702
Yeah, I mean, it's part of this.
是的，我的意思是，这是其中的一部分。

00:09:45.702 --> 00:09:56.179
We always talk about how there's this kind of second adolescence at the end of your 20s into your 30s, and it's maybe the more important one, and you're not really an adult yet then.
我们总是谈论在20多岁到30多岁时会有第二个青春期，这可能是更重要的一个，而那时你还不是真正的成年人。

00:09:56.179 --> 00:09:59.860
And I think this is one of those moments of like, what kind of grown up am I becoming?
我认为这是这样的时刻之一，我正在成为什么样的成年人？

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:04.539
Am I becoming the kind of grown up who can get screamed at on a Tuesday morning?
我是否正在成为那种在周二早上会被尖叫的成年人？

00:10:04.539 --> 00:10:06.539
And I'm just supposed to act like that's okay.
我应该表现得好像那没什么问题。

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:14.620
And it's such a glimpse into Barney's world and who he is, it is like, I got screamed at three times today, it's just like, do I want to live a life where that's normal?
这是对巴尼世界和他是谁的一瞥，就像，我今天被尖叫了三遍，就像，我想过一种正常的生活吗？

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:19.700
The shot where they introduced Blowman and Billson, is Brian's character Billson?
