I don't want to hear like, no, it was fine.
我不想听到这样的话，不，很好。

00:57:55.619 --> 00:58:00.539
It was, you know, yeah, I want to hear like, Oh, God, it was so hot.
你知道，是的，我想听到这样的话，哦，上帝，太热了。

00:58:00.539 --> 00:58:02.179
The sun is so bright in the desert.
沙漠里的阳光是那么的耀眼。

00:58:02.820 --> 00:58:07.820
Like I just tell me what's kind of obvious and yeah.
就像我只是告诉我什么是显而易见的，是的。

00:58:08.650 --> 00:58:24.800
And then you get into these other interviews, this other level, which is you ask yourself, how am I going to do this and not look like an asshole and not say something wrong and I'm going to just take my time and I'm going to be honest.
然后你进入其他面试，这个另一个层面，你问自己，我要怎么做，才不会看起来像个混蛋，也不会说错话，我会慢慢来，我会诚实。

00:58:24.800 --> 00:58:26.480
I'm gonna just be honest.
我会说实话。

00:58:26.480 --> 00:58:32.960
And then when I left that Brabiglia interview, I got and they sent a car for me, which was totally unnecessary.
然后当我离开布拉比利亚采访时，他们给我派了一辆车，这是完全没有必要的。

00:58:33.880 --> 00:58:43.800
But I got in the car and I'm like, the thing I said about being jealous of people with kids at home, that they're not gonna use that.
但我上了车，我就想，我说过嫉妒家里有孩子的人，他们不会使用这个。

00:58:43.800 --> 00:58:47.360
That's just, I thought, that's way too depressing.
只是，我想，这太令人沮丧了。

00:58:49.039 --> 00:58:51.119
And I thought it's depressing.
我认为这很令人沮丧。

00:58:51.119 --> 00:58:53.480
Well, it wasn't and people liked it.
嗯，事实并非如此，人们喜欢它。

00:58:53.480 --> 00:59:19.639
I thought what I thought was depressing about it was we all see people who've had long careers oftentimes in LA We see them at the grocery store and they have where I saw you I saw you with the gelsons a couple years ago I don't know if you're sure But yeah, and they have shitty shitty clothes on and dirty hat and and you some part of you is like Are they?
我觉得令人沮丧的是，我们经常在洛杉矶看到那些有着长期职业生涯的人，我们在杂货店看到他们，他们就在我见过你的地方，几年前我看到你和凝胶森，我不知道你是否确定，但是，是的，他们穿着破烂的衣服，戴着肮脏的帽子，而你的某些部分就像他们是吗？

00:59:19.639 --> 00:59:21.679
Did they not make any money at all?
难道他们根本就没有赚到钱吗？

00:59:21.679 --> 00:59:23.563
They never renegotiate.
他们从不重新谈判。

00:59:23.563 --> 00:59:29.869
You know, the three stooges, I heard a story, what's they never renegotiated.
你知道，三个傀儡，我听过一个故事，他们从未重新谈判过什么。

00:59:29.869 --> 00:59:30.688
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

00:59:30.688 --> 00:59:34.946
I mean, they were children of the depression, right?
我的意思是，他们是大萧条时期的孩子，对吗？

00:59:34.946 --> 00:59:46.002
So they got this contract to do these shorts and they just were so afraid of ever asking for a penny more that they never renegotiated.
所以他们拿到了制作这些短裤的合同，但他们只是害怕再多要一分钱，所以他们从未重新谈判。

00:59:46.002 --> 00:59:49.360
Like you assholes, you know, and come on.
就像你们这些混蛋一样，你知道，来吧。

00:59:49.360 --> 00:59:55.960
They should have pretended to be the three most powerful Hollywood agents, and that would have hurt death.
他们应该假装自己是好莱坞最有权势的三位特工，那样会伤人的。

00:59:55.960 --> 01:00:07.809
So my point is simply that that's sad that this guy who's had success in his career and has kids and now they're grown.
所以我的观点很简单，这个在职业生涯中取得成功并有孩子的人现在他们已经长大了，这是令人悲伤的。

01:00:07.809 --> 01:00:17.010
And I think he has enough money to live pretty well and people respect him like he envies something that he cannot have back.
我认为他有足够的钱过上很好的生活，人们尊重他，就像他羡慕一些他无法收回的东西一样。

01:00:17.010 --> 01:00:18.010
I don't know.
我不知道。

01:00:18.010 --> 01:00:19.010
Yeah.
是的。

01:00:19.010 --> 01:00:20.010
Well, I guess I could.
嗯，我想我可以。

01:00:20.010 --> 01:00:26.809
I'd have to divorce my wife and marry my assistant, but I don't have an assistant.
我必须与我的妻子离婚并与我的助理结婚，但我没有助理。

01:00:26.809 --> 01:00:49.369
I think that where it went, kind of viral the way it did, like I talked like three separate dad friends sent me that clip, like it landed on dads, I think, because there's something about, you know, showbiz is insane and it makes you unhappy in totally different ways no matter what stage you're at.
我认为它的传播方式就像病毒一样，就像我说的那样，就像三个不同的爸爸朋友发给我那个剪辑一样，就像它落在爸爸们身上一样，我想，因为有一些东西，你知道，演艺圈很疯狂，无论你处于哪个阶段，它都会以完全不同的方式让你不开心。

01:00:49.369 --> 01:01:13.889
It's like there's always a new way to be unhappy and to think you're not doing great and there's new, and I think in some ways the expectation is you ask an actor like who are you jealous of and it's like Tom Cruise, like they want you to say some person, but what you were really saying was like the most special time of your life is when you have something in front of that needs you to keep it alive, and that you know what your mission on Earth is.
好像总有一种新的方式让你不快乐，觉得自己做得不好，但有新的东西，我认为在某些方面，人们的期望是你问一个演员，比如你嫉妒谁，就像汤姆·克鲁斯，他们想让你说某个人，但你真正说的是你生命中最特别的时刻，就是当你面前有一些东西需要你让它活下去，你知道你在地球上的使命是什么。

01:01:13.889 --> 01:01:25.570
Like, that's when I found so moving about it, was it was like, and it's very kind of in the world of how I met your mother, that this kind of like, Ted is trying to love his kids by telling these stories.
就像，就在那时，我发现这件事非常感人，就好像，在我遇见你母亲的世界里，就像是，特德试图通过讲述这些故事来爱他的孩子们。

01:01:25.570 --> 01:01:37.289
He's trying to love them, he's trying to teach them, and he's also asking for their love and approval back in certain ways, but I just wanna commend you for, I know that that quote is gonna be around for a while, but yeah.
他试图爱他们，他试图教导他们，他也在以某些方式请求他们的爱和认可，但我只是想赞扬你，我知道这句话会流传一段时间，但是是的。

01:01:37.289 --> 01:02:18.655
No, but those are the things that people really I think makes them sit up and pay attention is when honesty cuts through the noise Yeah, I think you're right I think it's a good way if you ever find yourself in those interviews and This is sort of one of them, but the point is you know It's a longer interview and you're talking to people your respect and they're not they don't they don't want those canned answers that you know the the the go-to is just think honestly about the question and see if you can say something clearer clearly and a straightforward way.
不，但这些是人们真正让他们坐起来并注意的事情，当诚实消除噪音时是的，我认为你是对的，如果你发现自己在这些采访中，这是一个好方法，这就是其中之一，但重点是你知道这是一个较长的采访，你正在与你尊敬的人交谈，他们不是他们不想要那些你知道的罐装答案，最重要的是诚实地思考问题看看你是否能说得更清楚、更直接。

01:02:18.655 --> 01:02:24.063
You know I had so many dads tell me they're in the middle of it right now.
你知道有很多爸爸告诉我他们现在正处于困境之中。

01:02:24.063 --> 01:02:29.033
They have a two-year-old and a five-year-old and you know it's hard.
他们有一个两岁和一个五岁的孩子，你知道这很难。

01:02:29.033 --> 01:02:29.983
I mean it is.
我的意思是确实如此。

01:02:29.983 --> 01:02:35.830
You get so my neighbors have a little guy who he's like our practice grandchild.
你知道我的邻居有一个小家伙，他就像我们练习的孙子。

01:02:35.830 --> 01:03:05.210
He's such a great guy and he has this virus that little kids get and he's so upset and I just saw the dad this morning we were both walking our dogs and I went there yesterday to say hi to him and they like he has this thing I'm like okay I will come in you know cuz I don't want to get back and they had the worst night of their lives and those nights and And it's like, do you have two kids or three?
他是一个很棒的人，他感染了小孩子感染的病毒，他非常沮丧，我今天早上刚看到他爸爸，我们都在遛狗，我昨天去那里向他打招呼，他们喜欢他有这种东西，我想好吧，我会进来你知道的，因为我不想回来，他们度过了一生中最糟糕的一晚，那些夜晚，就像，你有两个孩子还是三个孩子？

01:03:05.210 --> 01:03:08.769
I mean, come on, those moments are like brutal.
我的意思是，来吧，那些时刻就像残酷的。

01:03:08.769 --> 01:03:19.210
So I've had a number of parents who are younger say, I was glad to hear somebody say that and remind me that I should remember that perspective.
所以我有很多年轻的父母说，我很高兴听到有人这么说，并提醒我应该记住这个观点。

01:03:19.210 --> 01:03:21.610
Oh, Bob, that's how I took it, honestly.
哦，鲍勃，老实说，我就是这么认为的。

01:03:21.610 --> 01:03:29.210
It was the opposite of sad to me because it was like, here's this guy that is very successful and artistic successful and respected.
对我来说，这与悲伤相反，因为这就像，这个人非常成功，在艺术上取得了成功并受到尊重。

01:03:29.210 --> 01:03:31.650
And he, he, he missed it.
而他，他，他错过了。

01:03:31.650 --> 01:03:39.289
It's none of that has, has, you served at the bigger joy of your life, which was, I loved you said, you knew what you were doing every day of your life.
这一切都没有，你为你的生活带来了更大的快乐，那就是，我爱你说的，你知道你生命中的每一天都在做什么。

01:03:39.289 --> 01:03:41.329
You knew what your job was.
你知道你的工作是什么。

01:03:41.329 --> 01:03:44.130
And I think that's, we were talking about development hell earlier.
我认为我们之前讨论过开发地狱。

01:03:44.130 --> 01:03:48.530
And I think part of what was nice about how much a mother is we knew where we were going for a decade.
我认为，作为一个母亲，我们知道这十年我们要去哪里，这是一件好事。

01:03:48.530 --> 01:03:50.929
And that is more akin to a family and parenting.
这更类似于家庭和养育子女。

01:03:50.929 --> 01:03:55.329
You know what you're doing every day for a decade when you're with those children and you're just attuned to them.
当你和这些孩子们在一起时，你知道十年来你每天在做什么，并且你只是适应他们。

01:03:55.329 --> 01:03:59.610
You're clearly a very good and loving dad, like that you want that job.
你显然是一个非常好的、慈爱的父亲，所以你想要这份工作。

01:03:59.610 --> 01:04:04.050
You wanted that job, you knew what that job was when you had it, and you miss it now.
你想要那份工作，当你拥有那份工作时你知道那份工作是什么，但现在你却怀念它。

01:04:04.050 --> 01:04:10.010
And I honestly felt like when I saw that clip, I was like looking at my phone on the weekend or something, probably my daughter was in the other room.
老实说，当我看到那个剪辑时，我感觉就像在周末看手机或其他什么，可能我女儿在另一个房间。

01:04:10.010 --> 01:04:13.010
I put down my phone and went and hung out with my daughter, like, what are you drawing?
我放下手机，去和女儿一起出去玩，比如，你在画什么？

01:04:13.010 --> 01:04:13.849
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

01:04:13.849 --> 01:04:15.250
I was like, just like, welcome me up.
我就像，就像，欢迎我。

01:04:15.250 --> 01:04:19.170
And I was like, remember, don't miss these moments.
我当时想，记住，不要错过这些时刻。

01:04:19.170 --> 01:04:20.730
So thank you for that, honestly.
所以说实话，谢谢你。

01:04:20.730 --> 01:05:09.065
And the thing is, my kids are at an age where everyone talks about your college age, like they don't want me around like my kids are an age where they like they are adults like you want to say hey do you remember when you were a kid remember who I remember I was a parent do you remember that because I don't I don't think you remember it at all it was actually a long time you were there you were there like they are at that they're are so far into adulthood now, their sense of self and their self-responsibility towards themselves in the world that you really go like, wow, that's just so long gone.
事情是这样的，我的孩子们正处在一个每个人都在谈论你的大学年龄的年龄，就像他们不希望我在身边一样，就像我的孩子们是一个他们喜欢自己是成年人的年龄，就像你想说的那样，嘿，你还记得当你还是个孩子的时候，还记得我是谁吗？在这个世界上对自己负责，你真的会想，哇，那已经过去了。

01:05:09.065 --> 01:05:11.715
And almost like it didn't happen.
几乎就好像这件事没有发生一样。

01:05:11.715 --> 01:05:13.160
But I know it did.
但我知道确实如此。

01:05:13.160 --> 01:05:18.058
The other thing I'll say is I was the second oldest of seven.
我要说的另一件事是我是七个孩子中第二大的。

01:05:18.058 --> 01:05:24.000
And so I was very entertained and enjoyed my younger brothers and sisters.
所以我很开心，也很喜欢我的弟弟妹妹们。

01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:26.367
And we're all still very close.
我们仍然非常亲密。

01:05:26.367 --> 01:05:30.719
And I knew when we had kids like this is going to be fun.
我知道当我们有了这样的孩子时会很有趣。

01:05:30.719 --> 01:05:32.762
I knew what kids were like.
我知道孩子们是什么样的。

01:05:32.762 --> 01:05:43.579
So I already, I wasn't, I was a little scared and there's still a lot to learn, but I wasn't completely, I mean, I knew how to change a diaper.
所以我已经，我不是，我有点害怕，还有很多东西要学，但我并不完全，我的意思是，我知道如何换尿布。

01:05:43.579 --> 01:05:48.118
You know, I mean, I was 14 when my youngest sister was born.
你知道，我的意思是，我最小的妹妹出生时我才 14 岁。

01:05:48.118 --> 01:05:52.051
And so I wasn't like, I was like, this can be great.
所以我不喜欢，我喜欢，这可能很棒。

01:05:52.051 --> 01:05:52.959
I love this.
我喜欢这个。

01:05:52.959 --> 01:05:56.817
And I, and I, I'm not saying I didn't lose my shit.
我，我，我并不是说我没有失去我的狗屎。

01:05:56.817 --> 01:05:58.103
Not I don't much.
不是我不多。

01:05:58.103 --> 01:06:03.550
But I, um, my bigger problem was, and this is a problem I've always had.
但我，嗯，我更大的问题是，这是我一直面临的问题。

01:06:03.550 --> 01:06:16.119
And this is probably why I'm in drama doing better as a drama actor than as a comedy which is that, when I even sort of look angry, I look really angry.
这可能就是为什么我在戏剧中作为一名戏剧演员比作为一名喜剧演员做得更好，因为当我看起来有点生气时，我看起来真的很生气。

01:06:16.119 --> 01:06:17.119
I look really angry.
我看起来真的很生气。

01:06:17.119 --> 01:06:20.920
Is that another Odin Kirk-ism?
这是另一种奥丁·柯克主义吗？

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:22.239
Is that another genetic Odin Kirk-ism?
这是另一种遗传的奥丁·柯克主义吗？

01:06:22.239 --> 01:06:24.000
It is, it is, my dad is that way.
是是是，我爸就是这样。

